# Shipping configuration for //shot:shot.
#
#   echo 'import("//build/args/shot-official.gn")' > out/ShotOfficial/args.gn
#   gn gen out/ShotOfficial
#   ninja -C out/ShotOfficial shot -j 12
#
# Why this file exists: every size number recorded in docs/size-attribution.md
# was measured on out/ShotCheck, which imports build/args/shot.gn only. That
# configuration is `is_debug = false` but NOT `is_official_build`, and the two
# are very different binaries:
#
#   build/config/dcheck_always_on.gni:
#     dcheck_always_on = (build_with_chromium && !is_official_build) || ...
#
# so the 336 MB baseline has every DCHECK compiled in -- condition, message and
# call -- and blink's layout and paint code is DCHECK-dense. And:
#
#   build/config/compiler/compiler.gni:74
#     use_thin_lto = is_cfi || (is_clang && is_official_build && ...)
#
# so it also has no cross-translation-unit inlining or dead-code elimination.
# (/OPT:REF and /OPT:ICF *are* already on -- build/config/win/BUILD.gn:196 turns
# them on for any `!is_debug && !is_component_build` build -- so the baseline is
# link-time dead-stripped. What is in it is genuinely reachable.)
#
# The point of this file is to measure that difference rather than argue about
# it: build the same tree both ways and diff the two images.

import("//build/args/shot.gn")

is_official_build = true

# Official Windows builds default chrome_pgo_phase to 2, which reads a profile
# from //chrome/build/pgo_profiles. That profile is a gclient-hook download for
# a Chrome build and is not in this checkout, and a profile collected on Chrome
# would describe a workload this binary does not run anyway.
chrome_pgo_phase = 0

# is_cfi and use_cfi_icall are Linux-x64-only in
# build/config/sanitizers/sanitizers.gni, so they stay off here and are not
# worth setting explicitly. Note that is_cfi would *increase* size.

# Deliberately NOT set here: optimize_for_size. It defaults to false on Windows
# (compiler.gni:98 turns it on only for Android/CastOS/Fuchsia), and it trades
# -O2 for a size-first pass. It is a separate measurement -- a screenshot tool
# has no throughput requirement worth defending, so it will probably be turned
# on, but on evidence rather than assumption.
